1
00:05:19,090 --> 00:05:25,090
A dream to save the wilderness. A secret that shocked the world.

2
00:10:38,181 --> 00:10:44,181
Grey Owl is a western, action, drama film directed by Richard Attenborough.

3
00:15:57,272 --> 00:16:03,272
Archie Grey Owl is a trapper in Canada in the early 1930s when a young
Iroquois woman from town asks him to teach her Indian ways.

4
00:21:16,363 --> 00:21:22,363
They live in the woods, where she is appalled at how trapped animals die.

5
00:26:35,454 --> 00:26:41,454
She adopts two orphaned beaver kits and helps
Archie see his way to stop trapping.

6
00:31:54,545 --> 00:32:00,545
Instead, he works as a guide, a naturalist writer, and then the Canadian government hires him to
save the beaver in a conserve by Lake Ajawaan in Prince Albert National Park.

7
00:37:13,636 --> 00:37:19,636
He writes a biography, which brings him attention in
Canada and invitations to lecture in England.

8
00:42:32,727 --> 00:42:38,727
Before he leaves, he and Anahareo (Pony) marry.

9
00:47:51,818 --> 00:47:57,818
In England, his secret is revealed.

10
00:53:10,909 --> 00:53:16,909
Will Anahareo continue to love him?

11
00:58:29,999 --> 00:58:35,999
Grey Owl, played by Pierce Brosnan.

12
01:03:49,090 --> 01:03:55,090
Cyrus Finney, played by Stewart Bick.

13
01:09:08,181 --> 01:09:14,181
Harry Champlin, played by Vlasta Vrana.

14
01:14:27,272 --> 01:14:33,272
Pony, played by Annie Galipeau.

15
01:19:46,363 --> 01:19:52,363
First Hunter, played by Neil Kroetsch.

16
01:25:05,454 --> 01:25:11,454
Second Hunter, played by Serge Houde.

17
01:30:24,545 --> 01:30:30,545
Grey Owl is a 1999 biographical film directed by Richard Attenborough and starring Pierce Brosnan in the role of real-life British schoolboy turned Native
American trapper "Grey Owl", Archibald Belaney (1888–1938), and Annie Galipeau as his wife Anahareo, with brief appearances by Graham Greene and others.

18
01:35:43,636 --> 01:35:49,636
The screenplay was written by William Nicholson.

19
01:41:02,727 --> 01:41:08,727
The film was released on 10 September 1999 in Spain and 15 February 2000 in US.

20
01:46:21,818 --> 01:46:27,818
It was the last film made by Largo Entertainment before it went defunct in 1999.

21
01:51:40,909 --> 01:51:46,909
The tone is emotional.
